<%# Dedicated Forecast V2 Inertia layout (spike slice A3).

  Layout decision (per blueprint "Layout Decision" and spec "Add a
  forecast-specific Inertia root template or layout"): Forecast V2 renders the
  Inertia/Vite/React workspace through a DEDICATED layout rather than the full
  app shell (`layouts/application`).

  Why dedicated, not the app shell:
  - The app shell pins a ~84px left nav, a ≤320px left account sidebar, AND a
    ≤400px right-side chat container. With the chat open the workspace is
    squeezed into a narrow middle column — exactly the "chat-width" concern the
    blueprint calls out. The Forecast V2 chart/scrub workspace needs the full
    content width.
  - The app shell's `_htmldoc` also mounts `turbo_frame_tag "modal"` /
    `turbo_frame_tag "drawer"` and Turbo morphing chrome around the page. We do
    NOT want Turbo to own modal/drawer/frame state inside the Inertia root; the
    React client owns ephemeral interaction state instead.

  What this layout still preserves (the auth/privacy chrome the blueprint
  requires) by reusing `shared/_htmldoc` (which renders `shared/_head`):
  - CSRF meta tags + CSP meta tag.
  - Tailwind design-system stylesheet + functional tokens.
  - Dark-mode check + privacy-mode check (no-flash inline scripts).
  - Flash notification tray (`render_flash_notifications`).
  - `turbo_stream_from Current.family` for server-pushed family updates.
  - Authentication context: this layout is only served from controllers that
    inherit ApplicationController, so Current.user / Current.family are scoped.

  Vite asset loading follows the Vite Rails helpers' dev/prod split:
  - Development: `vite_client_tag` + `vite_react_refresh_tag` enable HMR and
    React Fast Refresh (both no-op outside the dev server).
  - Production: `vite_typescript_tag` resolves the compiled, fingerprinted
    entrypoint from the Vite build manifest produced during `assets:precompile`.

  The final dedicated-vs-shell decision record (desktop + mobile screenshots,
  the right-side-chat narrowness evidence) is captured in slice A8. %>
<%= render "layouts/shared/htmldoc" do %>
  <%# Full-width Inertia workspace root: no app nav, sidebars, or right-side
      chat so the Forecast V2 workspace gets the entire viewport width. %>
  <main id="main" class="h-full w-full overflow-y-auto bg-surface">
    <%= yield %>
  </main>

  <%# Vite client + React Refresh (development only; both render nothing in
      production), then the compiled Forecast entrypoint (production-resolved via
      the Vite manifest). Module scripts load correctly from the end of <body>. %>
  <%= vite_client_tag %>
  <%= vite_react_refresh_tag %>
  <%= vite_typescript_tag "forecast.tsx" %>
<% end %>
